# Single Task Focus

Each change does one task. Leave unrelated improvements for a separate task.

## Boundaries

- Modify only code that the current task requires.
- Leave unrelated refactors and improvements alone.
- Save other issues for their own tasks.
- Do not mix concerns from different features in one change.

## Edits

- Edit only the files the current task needs.
- Change only the lines the task needs.
- Skip formatting and style fixes outside the task.
- Do not clean up neighboring code because you are already in the file.

## Before finishing

- Check that each changed line belongs to the task.
- Remove unrelated changes.
- Split an unrelated improvement into its own task.
- Keep the change small.

## Violations

- Fixing an unrelated lint error.
- Updating an unrelated dependency.
- Reformatting code the task did not touch.
- Adding behavior beyond the task.

### Button handler

Task: fix the button click handler.

Do not also reformat the file, update dependencies, and fix typos in comments. Fix the handler. Save the rest.

### API endpoint

Task: add a new endpoint.

Bad: add the endpoint and rewrite an old one in the same change.

```javascript
function newEndpoint() {
  // Add endpoint
}

function oldEndpoint() {
  // Cleanup while here
}
```

Good: add only the new endpoint.

```javascript
function newEndpoint() {
  // Only add new endpoint
}
```
